{# auto-cost reference-bandwidth changes how interface bandwidth maps to OSPF cost, locally, per router. Unlike
   hello/area/network-type mismatches, OSPF does NOT reject the adjacency over a reference-bandwidth mismatch -
   IOS only logs a local warning. That's exactly what makes it dangerous in production: the network looks fully
   converged (every neighbor stays Full) while path costs silently diverge across routers. #}
router ospf 1
 auto-cost reference-bandwidth {{ 100 if rollback else 10000 }}
